.TH BENCHMARK\-STORAGE\-PTS 1 "February 2026" "benchmarking" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh \- benchmark storage I/O performance using the Phoronix Test Suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh
\fB\-\-disk\fR \fI"<device>;<label>"\fR
[\fB\-\-disk\fR \fI"<device>;<label>"\fR ...]
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh
\fB\-\-disk\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B WARNING: This script is destructive.
It formats and completely wipes all data on every target disk before testing.
.PP
Benchmarks storage I/O across one or more disks sequentially.
For each disk the script formats it with XFS, mounts it, runs the full PTS
storage test suite, and saves results before moving on to the next disk.
Tests are never run in parallel across disks to avoid I/O contention.
.PP
The test suite covers latency, IOPS, throughput, and workload characterisation
across multiple access patterns, block sizes, I/O engines, and read/write ratios.
.PP
.B SSD steady-state preconditioning
is performed by default before formatting each SSD or NVMe device.
The script writes across the full device twice (128\ KiB blocks, queue depth\ 32)
to move it through its garbage-collection and wear-levelling cycle so that
measurements reflect steady-state performance rather than a rested state.
Preconditioning is skipped automatically for HDDs and unknown device types,
and can be disabled with \fB\-\-skip\-preconditioning\fR.
.PP
PTS is installed automatically on supported distributions (Ubuntu, Debian,
Rocky Linux, openSUSE) if not already present.
.PP
Results are collected into
.B ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/
relative to the directory from which the script is invoked.
.SH PTS TESTS
.TP
.B pts/fio
Flexible I/O tester.
Covers sequential and random read/write, multiple I/O engines (sync, psync,
Linux AIO, io_uring), direct and buffered I/O, and block sizes from 512\ B to 8\ MB.
.TP
.B pts/dbench
Filesystem metadata throughput using CIFS-style workloads.
.TP
.B pts/fs\-mark
Filesystem throughput benchmark focused on file creation and deletion patterns.
.TP
.B pts/compilebench
Simulates kernel compilation I/O patterns (requires Python\ 2; skipped automatically
when only Python\ 3 is available).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Disk target options (at least one required)
.TP
.B \-\-disk " " \fI"<device>;<label>"\fR
Add a target disk.
.I device
is the block device path (e.g.\&
.BR /dev/vdb ).
.I label
is a short name used for the mount point
.RB ( /mnt/<label> )
and result directory names.
The argument must be quoted so the shell does not interpret
.RB ' ; '
as a command separator.
May be repeated for multiple disks.
.TP
.B \-\-disk\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Read disk entries from a file, one
.I device;label
entry per line.
Lines beginning with
.RB ' # '
and blank lines are ignored.
May be combined with \fB\-\-disk\fR.
.SS General options
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-preconditioning
Skip SSD steady-state preconditioning passes.
Use when re-running tests immediately after a previous run (the device is
already conditioned) or when turnaround time matters more than strict
reproducibility.
.TP
.B \-\-upload
Upload results to OpenBenchmarking.org after the run completes.
Requires \fB\-\-result\-id\fR and \fB\-\-result\-name\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-result\-id " " \fIID\fR
Short identifier for the run (e.g.\&
.IR ceph\-dc1\-q1\-2026 ).
Used as the output directory name and the upload identifier on
OpenBenchmarking.org.
Default: auto-generated timestamp string.
.TP
.B \-\-result\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Human-readable display name for the result (e.g.\&
.IR "Ceph DC1 \- NVMe vs HDD Q1 2026" ).
Required when \fB\-\-upload\fR is specified.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display a help message and exit.
.SH DISK FILE FORMAT
One entry per line in the format
.IR device ; label .
Lines starting with
.RB ' # '
and blank lines are ignored.
.PP
.nf
.RS
# Storage benchmark disk list
/dev/vdb;NVMe_Replica3
/dev/vdc;NVMe_EC32

/dev/vdd;HDD_Replica3
/dev/vde;HDD_EC32
.RE
.fi
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.B ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/<result\-id>\-system\-snapshot.txt
System snapshot captured before the run.
.TP
.BI ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/<label>_ test _result/
One PTS result directory per (disk\~\[mu]\~test) combination (e.g.\&
.BR NVMe_Replica3_fio_result/ ,
.BR NVMe_Replica3_dbench_result/ ,
\&...).
Each contains
.B composite.xml
and all result data for that test on that disk.
.SH COMPARISON
When multiple disks are tested in a single run, a local comparison report is
generated at the end using
.BR "phoronix\-test\-suite compare\-results" .
.PP
To generate full reports in all formats across disks or across separate runs, use
.BR create\-report\-pts.sh (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Test two disks with different characteristics in a single run:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh \\
    \-\-disk "/dev/vdb;NVMe_Replica3" \\
    \-\-disk "/dev/vdc;HDD_Replica3"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Test from a disk file and upload results:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh \-\-disk\-file disks.conf \-\-upload \\
    \-\-result\-name "Ceph NVMe vs HDD \- Q1 2026" \\
    \-\-result\-id "ceph\-dc1\-q1\-2026"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Skip preconditioning for a quick re-run immediately after a previous run:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh \-\-disk\-file disks.conf \\
    \-\-skip\-preconditioning \\
    \-\-result\-id "ceph\-dc1\-q1\-2026\-rerun"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compare two separate runs (before and after a storage upgrade) using
.BR create\-report\-pts.sh (1):
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh \-\-disk "/dev/vdb;NVMe" \-\-result\-id "before\-upgrade"
\&./benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh \-\-disk "/dev/vdb;NVMe" \-\-result\-id "after\-upgrade"
\&./create\-report\-pts.sh \\
    ./benchmark\-results/before\-upgrade/ \\
    ./benchmark\-results/after\-upgrade/
.RE
.fi
